# Gitignored files copied into every new worktree.
#
# A worktree gets the tracked files for free. Anything deliberately kept out of
# version control has to be named here or it simply will not exist in the new
# tree — and the agent working there will not know it is missing.
#
# Build output and IDE state are excluded on purpose: they are per-tree by
# nature, regenerating them is correct, and copying them across would hand a
# fresh worktree a stale DerivedData to be confused by.

# The project instructions. Gitignored (.gitignore:25) yet 369 lines of how
# this repo actually works — the merge workflow, the CI lanes, the teardown
# ordering traps. Without it a parallel agent starts with no project context at
# all, which is the single most expensive thing to be missing.
CLAUDE.md

# Local maintenance script, untracked but referenced by the header workflow.
update_headers.py
